    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256">

                <pb facs="0209" n="197" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg197"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.Consultation(2)/52: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-23T11:00:00-03:00">June 23, 1940—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>301. For the Under Secretary. My telegram no. 299, June 22, 2 p.m.<anchor n="27"
                        xml:id="d256-f1"/> Aranha showed me telegrams from his missions in Chile,
                    Bolivia, Uruguay, Ecuador and Colombia expressing willingness to have conference
                    in Rio.</p>
                <p>He showed me also a telegram from his Legation at Habana received here the same
                    day that I received your circular telegram June 17, 10 a.m. conveying the
                    invitation of the Government of Cuba to the conference to be held at Habana. He
                    did not like that.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
